##
    A project that cannot say where its build goes.

    'output' names the folder a build is written into, and is the only way to say so — a loose
    source file has nowhere to record the answer, so it lands in the 'bin' beside it. Where a
    build goes is a thing a build says about itself, and this is the file that says things about
    a build.

    The first line names nothing. The third disagrees with the second, and a build is written to
    one place, so there is no answer to pick between them: whichever were chosen, half the file
    would be wrong.
##

project Unclear
    source ../runtime/overflow.pc
    output
    output here
    output there
end project
